  "levels_won_this_session": [],
  "novel_mechanics_found": "Level 7 confirms that the central color-1 fixture pins individual strokes independently: an obstructed horizontal stroke can remain fixed while a vertical stroke and selection marker continue moving, separating a plus into offset strokes. Rectangle collisions are perimeter-preserving resizes in exact 3-pixel quanta (13x13 -> 16x10, and the inverse sequence -> 7x19). The intended level-7 color assignment was decoded from all targets, including the initially overlooked fourth color-8 socket: the 37-pixel-wide plus fits the four color-8 sockets, the small plus fits the three color-11 sockets after asymmetric deformation, and the rectangle resizes to 19x7 for the two color-9 sockets.",
  "narrative": "Resolved the exact 341-action prefix and replayed it from a fresh env.reset(); frame.levels_completed reached 6 before exploration. Frame-only interaction on level 7 decoded per-stroke pinning, exact rectangle perimeter exchange, the hidden assignment constraint, and routes that separately placed the color-8 and color-11 pieces. An early wrong assignment and a color-14 repaint trap consumed too much of the per-level move bar; during the final 19x7 color-9 rectangle route, action 650 returned an empty terminal frame with levels_completed=0. No level-7 win was observed. I stopped because the live attempt had irreversibly timed out and the remaining 150-call session budget could not replay the 341-action prefix or run reproduce(); the preserved action_sequence is the full reset-to-level-6 prefix, so reproduction_verified is honestly false for this session.",
  "gotchas": [
    "The level-7 color-8 sockets are at (9,9), (3,15), (39,15), and (9,27); the far-right (39,15) socket is easy to overlook and invalidates the tempting 7x19 color-8 rectangle assignment.",
    "The likely intended assignment is big plus -> color 8, small plus -> color 11, rectangle -> color 9. The rectangle's exact color-9 target geometry is 19x7, spanning the sockets near (39,24) and (57,18).",
    "For the big plus, a useful color-8 goal geometry is horizontal x=3..39 at y=15 plus vertical x=9 at y=9..27. The fixture can pin the horizontal stroke while moving the vertical stroke independently.",
    "A 13x13 rectangle preserves its 48-pixel perimeter when resized: one collision changes it to 16x10; repeated inverse side collisions produce 7x19. Four collisions from 7x19 should produce 19x7.",
    "Paint contact is hazardous during separated-stroke transit: moving a vertical stroke along the top swatches can repaint an otherwise correctly placed piece to color 14. Drop the stroke below y=5 before returning horizontally.",
    "The row-63 bar is a real level timer, not merely decorative. Exhausting it returned an empty terminal frame and levels_completed=0; route and assignment experiments must be minimized.",
    "ACTION5 cycles small plus -> rectangle -> big plus -> small plus. ACTION1/2/3/4 are up/down/left/right in 3-pixel quanta.",
    "Rendered frame buffers mutate in place, so copy grids before computing action diffs."
  ],
